===============================================================================

                     Zombie Attack source code documentation
			        
                 This source code should be managed in Eclipse 3.4+

===============================================================================

How to setup Eclipse for this project?
--------------------------------------

1. First you must have configured Eclipse enviroment.
   Configuration of Eclipse on different platform is task for you,
   go to http://www.eclipse.org/.

2. In Eclipse you could open this project by 
   "File->Import->General->Existing projects into workspace".

3. After this you must setup couple of things, like 
   "Build Configuration" propertly for your platform.
   You could do this throught "Project->Build Configuration->Set Active",
   and choosing Linux or Windows. 
   
4. Now you could build the project by "Project->Build All" or "Ctrl+B"

5. Last thing is setup run arguments. Go to "Run->Run Configurations..." 
   and double click on "Local C/C++ Application". Select newly created
   run configuration and go to the "Arguments" tab. Paste this to 
   the "Program arguments" text field:
	-window
	-fps
	-datadir ${workspace_loc:AtakZombie}/Data
	-localedir ${workspace_loc:AtakZombie}/i18n

6. Now you could run program "Run->Run" or "Ctrl+F11".


File names notation
-------------------

Most of the files have prefixes. This prefixes describe role of the 
content's objects:

Prefix:    Description:
l_         Layers are updated and draw on the screen in main loop. 
m_         Managers are loops to control group of layers in the main loop
s_         Subsystems take care of some elements of game, 
           like playing audio buffers.

Every layers has his own API and manager should take every layer differently. 
Pair of manager and layers uses subsystems to make some stuff like render fonts
or play sound.            

